A||N||2||Black87GT||How much horsepower has a 3.1 V6||||1||
Z||000000||Black87GT||12-03-2001||11:10 AM||||I recently bought a 87 GT 3.1 V6. It has a manual 5-speed transmission. <P>Does anyone know how much horsepower is in there.  According to the dealer (who has 15 years of fiero experience including tuning) it is about 160 HP.  <P>Does ayone know if this is true and is there anyway to add a few more horses under the hood? (I already have a black bomber to replace my CAT).<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||12-03-2001||02:23 PM||||Depends on what the 3.1 came out of.  Fieros never came with a 3.1 from the factory.  If it's an OEM 3.1, you're probably looking at about 150hp?  If it's a Fiero 2.8 that's had a 3.1 crank you could be a bit higher, since the Fiero has a slightly bigger cam than the stock 3.1 (I think).  <P>Someone correct me if I'm wrong.  Also, I know the Fiero has the highest performance iron 2.8 heads.  I don't know if these are the same on the 3.1.  The 3.4 iron heads are the same as teh Fiero 2.8 heads.<P>Sorry for the confusion - I guess it all comes back to "what kind of 3.1 is it?"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black87GT||12-03-2001||03:02 PM||||Well, I don't know if it was a 2.8 converted to a 3.1 or if it is just a 3.1 V6.<P>I also had the option of buying a 3.4 V6 because the engine needed to be replaced anyway, but that was about $1200 more, so I decided to stick with the 3.1 because it is more compatible with the original fiero parts(correct me if i am wrong).<P>maybe my fiero will be not as fast as some other cars but I am sure it will turn a few heads when I cruise down the streets.<P>||||reg||1
